      "writtenOn": "2022-01-27T08:09:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "UNCHANGED:  APTX_CHANNEL_UNCHANGED value may indicate that the caller may want to change one or more aptX Configuration values but wants the Channel Mode to remain at its existing value – this saves the API user from having to recover the current value and fill it in. A default setting when the channel configuration is unknown\n\nJOINT_STEREO / TWS_STEREO: Two channels processed together in a single stream\nMONO / DUAL_MONO / TWS_MONO: \nMONO:A mono channel in a single stream\nDUAL_MONO: Two mono channels in multiplexed streams (TWS) \nEARBUD: Two mono channels in interleaved streams (TWS+)\n\nIs there anything specific to QCOM TWS+ that the source side handles the earbuds left / right sides respectively?\nYes, TWS+ L and R are having different connection.",
